{
  "evals": [
    {
      "id": "triage-device-assert",
      "prompt": "Our managed two-node Cosmos3 reasoner training job cosmos3-reasoner-train-7c41d2 stopped and SLURM reports it COMPLETED. Its artifacts are in the skill's assets/managed_job_failures/device_assert directory: the Cosmos job record, the sacct output, the job's stdout and the Framework status.json. Diagnose it only: do not fix anything, do not resubmit, and do not edit those files. Write outputs/diagnosis.json with the fields job_id, scheduler_state, actual_outcome, root_cause, failure_class (infra or program), retry (true or false), next_action and evidence (a list of file:line quotes), and explain the reasoning in outputs/diagnosis.md.",
      "expected_outcome": "The diagnosis recognises that SLURM's COMPLETED hides a failed training step, identifies the CUDA device-side assert (index out of bounds) as the root cause with the NCCL watchdog timeouts as downstream symptoms, classifies it as a program failure with no retry, and proposes a data/label investigation instead of a resubmission.",
      "assertions": [
        "outputs/diagnosis.json reports scheduler_state COMPLETED but an actual failed outcome, citing the failed srun step (4815162.0, exit 1) and the FAILURE line of status.json",
        "The root cause is the CUDA device-side assert (index out of bounds in IndexKernel.cu) on rank 5; the NCCL watchdog timeouts are identified as downstream symptoms, not the cause",
        "failure_class is program and retry is false; next_action investigates the data or labels (for example with CUDA_LAUNCH_BLOCKING=1 or dataset validation) rather than resubmitting",
        "Nothing was resubmitted and the files under assets/managed_job_failures were not modified",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {"path": "outputs/diagnosis.json", "min_bytes": 200},
        {"path": "outputs/diagnosis.md", "min_bytes": 300},
        {"path": "result_summary.md", "min_bytes": 100},
        {"path": "transcript.md", "min_bytes": 300}
      ],
      "stages": ["collect evidence", "classify", "report"]
    },
    {
      "id": "triage-gpu-fell-off-bus",
      "prompt": "Our managed two-node Cosmos3 reasoner training job cosmos3-reasoner-train-a19f03 failed after about two hours. Its artifacts are in the skill's assets/managed_job_failures/gpu_fell_off_bus directory: the Cosmos job record, the sacct output, the job's stdout, the Framework status.json and the node epilog's dmesg capture. Diagnose it only: do not fix anything, do not resubmit, and do not edit those files. Write outputs/diagnosis.json with the fields job_id, scheduler_state, actual_outcome, root_cause, failure_class (infra or program), retry (true or false), next_action and evidence (a list of file:line quotes), and explain the reasoning in outputs/diagnosis.md, including exactly how a retry should be submitted if you recommend one.",
      "expected_outcome": "The diagnosis identifies Xid 79 (GPU fallen off the bus) on gpu-b032 as the root cause, with the CUDA launch failure and NCCL errors as downstream symptoms, classifies it as an infrastructure failure that may be retried, and describes a retry under a new job record with retry_of set, fresh output paths and a node exclusion checked against the live inventory, without submitting it.",
      "assertions": [
        "The root cause is the Xid 79 'GPU has fallen off the bus' event on gpu-b032 from the epilog dmesg capture; the 'unspecified launch failure' traceback and NCCL system error are identified as downstream symptoms",
        "failure_class is infra and retry is true",
        "The proposed retry uses a new job record with retry_of cosmos3-reasoner-train-a19f03 (the old record marked ERROR with ERR_INFRA), fresh result and checkpoint paths, and excludes gpu-b032 only after checking the live node inventory",
        "Nothing was resubmitted and the files under assets/managed_job_failures were not modified",
        "The skill's documented workflow executed without errors on the first attempt"
      ],
      "checks": [
        {"path": "outputs/diagnosis.json", "min_bytes": 200},
        {"path": "outputs/diagnosis.md", "min_bytes": 300},
        {"path": "result_summary.md", "min_bytes": 100},
        {"path": "transcript.md", "min_bytes": 300}
      ],
      "stages": ["collect evidence", "classify", "retry proposal", "report"]
    }
  ],
  "credentials": [],
  "gpus": 1,
  "budget": {"minutes": 15, "tokens": 800000}
}
